WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.375
For the I S S O, this is
the closure evidence.

2
00:00:03.375 --> 00:00:08.611
A finding closed only after a re-read
showed the intended state, with the query,

3
00:00:08.611 --> 00:00:11.719
the time, a hash of the
response and the checker,

4
00:00:11.719 --> 00:00:14.337
which is the workbook's closure clause,

5
00:00:14.337 --> 00:00:21.455
and it supports NIST SP 800-53's
configuration change control, CM-3,

6
00:00:21.455 --> 00:00:26.363
and the monitoring for unauthorized
change that NIST SP 800-37 calls for.

7
00:00:26.363 --> 00:00:31.326
No person can close a finding by setting
its state, which is separation of duties.

8
00:00:31.326 --> 00:00:33.825
A read that predates the
change doesn't count.

9
00:00:33.825 --> 00:00:37.522
And an empty intended state
never closes anything:

10
00:00:37.522 --> 00:00:40.320
a verified change, not an asserted one.
